The latter had too complicated theory of group monster generation. They 
obviously are created when more than two generating particles collide at 
the same time.

By observing the rate difference of single monster generation and group 
monster generation we can deduct how many collisions happen just between 
two particles and how many happen between more than two particles. From 
this we can make statistical picture of the particle void and what kind 
of forces govern the particle movement.

One observation is that the character's position on the level repel 
particles on the upper void, so these voids between levels are not 
totally unconnected from the effects on the levels.

